  "notes": [
    "Source: supplied Hammer product CSV filtered to vendor == TandT; audited against all 128 items from shared/seed/items.ts. Names, units and brand only; no raw price observations, retailer pages or UPC confirmation available.",
    "Conservative exact-package audit. Assignments list manually checked product identity and explicit catalogue-sized packs. No 15% size tolerance is assumed: 630g vs 650g, 1.54L/1.75L vs 1.75L/1.89L, 227g vs 250g, 8.2kg vs 8kg, etc. are excluded rather than treated as equivalent. Organic, enriched egg claims, flavoured/protein drinks, reduced sodium and uncertain variants are withheld to avoid blending distinct price histories. Catalogue is unbranded, so ordinary named grocery brands are allowed.",
    "All auto-matched rows outside assignments are excluded: processed foods sharing an ingredient word, different pack/variant, and missing or ambiguous package metadata. This is an allowlist for the supplied matcher, not a claim that every exclusion is intrinsically bad merchandise. Nonmatching unrelated groceries are left alone. Explicit shampoo/conditioner/toothpaste rows are excluded too.",
    "Egg count suffixes such as 12pcs, 18pcs and 30pcs are not reliably parsed by the supplied matcher. The explicit 18pcs white large egg row is assigned to eggs-large-18, not the default eggs-large-12. Unknown count and 30pcs rows are excluded.",
    "Vegetable oil 3L rows are explicitly assigned to vegetable-oil-3l; the canola item has a broad vegetable oil alias and otherwise wins a tie incorrectly.",
    "Known good candidates blocked by supplied matcher: TandT76357201/TandT78945301 (2% milk 4L), TandT76360201/TandT76359501 (2% milk 2L): partly skimmed is rejected as skim by the 2% rule and misassigned to skim. They remain excluded until matcher is fixed. TandT60271101 (Robin Hood Flour Allpurpose 5kg), TandT60251901 (Quaker Large Flake 1kg), TandT60602601/TandT74753901 (540mL red kidney beans), TandT60286101/TandT74755101 (170g flaked light tuna), TandT63095601 (341mL Green Giant Niblets corn), TandT63720201 (12pcs large brown eggs) also need matcher vocabulary/variant fixes and are not forced assignments.",
    "Fresh produce sold in weighted bags/boxes cannot be mapped to per-kg catalogue prices without knowing whether the raw price is for the package or per-weight. Examples: Gala apples, navel oranges, cabbage, zucchini, vine tomatoes, red grapes and sweet potatoes. Missing fresh matches are recorded as blocked, not silently normalized. A ginger row explicitly labelled (lb)/lb is included, but its raw-price basis and importer lb-to-kg conversion must be verified before use.",
    "Each produce: a whole head/stalk/bunch is treated as the normal single sales unit for cauliflower, celery, kale, iceberg lettuce and green onions. Ambiguous bagged garlic/avocados/limes and romaine hearts with unknown count are excluded; an English cucumber 3pcs is not a single cucumber.",
    "No prices, date coverage, availability, geographical package differences, organic parity, or identity across hashed and TandT-prefixed IDs were verified. Assignments preserve every ID independently and do not deduplicate regional/old records.",
    "Audit counts: 13,581 distinct TandT product IDs; 767 auto-matched under supplied matcher; 97 safe assignments covering 56/128 catalogue items; 675 exclusions (670 unsafe/uncertain auto-matches plus 5 explicit non-grocery products). All assignments pass the supplied matcher; 5 default-routing mistakes corrected (18-egg row plus 4 vegetable oil rows). Remaining 72 items have no verified exact safe assignment in this file, not proven unavailable at the chain."
  ]
